  src/ui/tasks.js     task list + the add/edit form
  src/ui/bell.js      bell, unread count, dropdown panel
  src/ui/toast.js     transient banner when a reminder fires while you're looking
  src/os-notify.js    optional layer: permission, mirror active reminders to Notification API
  test/              unit tests against reminders.js / tasks.js

  Two boundaries worth calling out:

  - [1m[38;5;153mreminders.js[39m never touches the DOM, the clock, or storage.[0m It takes state and [38;5;153mnow[39m and returns what should be
    showing. Every interesting rule — including the dismissal-key rule we discussed — lives there, so every interesting
    rule is unit-testable by passing a fake [38;5;153mnow[39m. No [38;5;153mjsdom[39m, no fake timers.
  - [1m[38;5;153mscheduler.js[39m is the only thing that knows real time exists.[0m It ticks (~every 15s, which is plenty for
    minute-resolution reminders), and critically it re-checks on [38;5;153mvisibilitychange[39m and [38;5;153mfocus[39m so that coming back to a
    backgrounded tab catches up immediately rather than waiting out the interval. Browsers throttle timers in background
    tabs, so the catch-up is load-bearing, not a nicety.

  [38;5;153mos-notify.js[39m is deliberately a leaf that nothing else imports from — the app works identically with the file deleted.
  That's what keeps the "in-page is the source of truth" promise structural rather than aspirational.

  Since this repo has no tooling configured at all, now is the cheapest moment to decide what to set up.
